paragraph(rel,'To eliminate unphysical synthesis',r'''Ground-truth database sampling, introduced in SECOND~\cite{yan2018second}, enriches underrepresented classes by inserting object point clouds into training scenes. Placement can nevertheless introduce ground-height inconsistencies, collisions with background structures, or unrealistic point densities at the target range. Our Physics-Consistent Ground-Truth Augmentation (\texttt{PC-GTA}, Section~\ref{sec:pc_gta}) combines local ground-height estimation, static obstacle clearance, and range-adaptive point subsampling. LOS rejection, shadow masking, and radiometric adjustment are optional implementation mechanisms and were disabled in the primary run. The historical sampler comparisons change complete recipes, including sampling probability and insertion quotas, so their AP differences do not isolate any single physical constraint.''')
